--- LST2-15/16/17/18/19/23: list properties, a three-element list ---
a list called cupboard is [534, 171, 947].
If cupboard's length is not 3 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-15: expected 3 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length.
If cupboard's size is not cupboard's length then, Print "ASSERT LST2-16: expected {cupboard's length} got {cupboard's size}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's size.
If cupboard's empty then, Print "ASSERT LST2-17: expected 0 got {cupboard's empty}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's empty.
If cupboard's first is not 534 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-18: expected 534 got {cupboard's first}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's first.
If cupboard's last is not 947 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-19: expected 947 got {cupboard's last}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's last.
If cupboard's first is not element 1 of cupboard then, Print "ASSERT LST2-23: expected {element 1 of cupboard} got {cupboard's first}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's first.
If cupboard's last is not element 3 of cupboard then, Print "ASSERT LST2-23: expected {element 3 of cupboard} got {cupboard's last}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's last.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a list called cupboard is [534, 171, 947],
  If cupboard's length is not 3 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-15: expected 3 got {cupboard's length}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's length,
  If cupboard's size is not cupboard's length then, Print "ASSERT LST2-16: expected {cupboard's length} got {cupboard's size}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's size,
  If cupboard's empty then, Print "ASSERT LST2-17: expected 0 got {cupboard's empty}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's empty,
  If cupboard's first is not 534 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-18: expected 534 got {cupboard's first}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's first,
  If cupboard's last is not 947 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-19: expected 947 got {cupboard's last}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's last,
  If cupboard's first is not element 1 of cupboard then, Print "ASSERT LST2-23: expected {element 1 of cupboard} got {cupboard's first}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's first,
  If cupboard's last is not element 3 of cupboard then, Print "ASSERT LST2-23: expected {element 3 of cupboard} got {cupboard's last}", Exit 95. Print cupboard's last.

--- the same leaf, a single-element list (first, last and element 1 all agree) ---
a list called 'the dispatch note' is [117].
If 'the dispatch note's length is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-15: expected 1 got {'the dispatch note's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note's length.
If 'the dispatch note's size is not 'the dispatch note's length then, Print "ASSERT LST2-16: expected {'the dispatch note's length} got {'the dispatch note's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note's size.
If 'the dispatch note's empty then, Print "ASSERT LST2-17: expected 0 got {'the dispatch note's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note's empty.
If 'the dispatch note's first is not 117 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-18: expected 117 got {'the dispatch note's first}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note's first.
If 'the dispatch note's last is not 117 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-19: expected 117 got {'the dispatch note's last}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note's last.
If 'the dispatch note's first is not element 1 of 'the dispatch note' then, Print "ASSERT LST2-23: expected {element 1 of 'the dispatch note'} got {'the dispatch note's first}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note's first.
If 'the dispatch note's last is not element 1 of 'the dispatch note' then, Print "ASSERT LST2-23: expected {element 1 of 'the dispatch note'} got {'the dispatch note's last}", Exit 95. Print 'the dispatch note's last.

--- LST2-20: an empty list - length/size/empty without a flag, first/last with one ---
a list called 'the inbox' is [].
If 'the inbox's length is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-20: expected 0 got {'the inbox's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox's length.
If 'the inbox's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-20: expected 0 got {'the inbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox's size.
If 'the inbox's empty is false then, Print "ASSERT LST2-20: expected 1 got {'the inbox's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox's empty.
a boolean called 'the inbox found an error already pending' is false.
On error Set 'the inbox found an error already pending' to true.
a boolean called 'the inbox empty first read errored' is false.
a number called 'the inbox empty first read' is 'the inbox's first.
On error Set 'the inbox empty first read errored' to true.
If 'the inbox empty first read errored' is false then, Print "ASSERT LST2-20: expected 1 got {'the inbox empty first read errored'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox empty first read errored'.
If 'the inbox empty first read' is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-20: expected 0 got {'the inbox empty first read'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox empty first read'.
a boolean called 'the inbox empty last read errored' is false.
a number called 'the inbox empty last read' is 'the inbox's last.
On error Set 'the inbox empty last read errored' to true.
If 'the inbox empty last read errored' is false then, Print "ASSERT LST2-20: expected 1 got {'the inbox empty last read errored'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox empty last read errored'.
If 'the inbox empty last read' is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-20: expected 0 got {'the inbox empty last read'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox empty last read'.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a list called 'the inbox' is [],
  If 'the inbox's length is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-20: expected 0 got {'the inbox's length}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox's length,
  If 'the inbox's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-20: expected 0 got {'the inbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox's size,
