  On error Set 'the inbox found an error already pending' to true,
  a boolean called 'the inbox empty first read errored' is false,
  a number called 'the inbox empty first read' is 'the inbox's first,
  On error Set 'the inbox empty first read errored' to true,
  If 'the inbox empty first read errored' is false then, Print "ASSERT LST2-20: expected 1 got {'the inbox empty first read errored'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox empty first read errored',
  If 'the inbox empty first read' is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-20: expected 0 got {'the inbox empty first read'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox empty first read',
  a boolean called 'the inbox empty last read errored' is false,
  a number called 'the inbox empty last read' is 'the inbox's last,
  On error Set 'the inbox empty last read errored' to true,
  If 'the inbox empty last read errored' is false then, Print "ASSERT LST2-20: expected 1 got {'the inbox empty last read errored'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox empty last read errored',
  If 'the inbox empty last read' is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-20: expected 0 got {'the inbox empty last read'}", Exit 95. Print 'the inbox empty last read'.

--- LST2-21/22: element 1, plus a literal index at another position ---
a list called 'the greeting' is [151, 447, 765].
If element 1 of 'the greeting' is not 151 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-21: expected 151 got {element 1 of 'the greeting'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'the greeting'.
If element 3 of 'the greeting' is not 765 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-22: expected 765 got {element 3 of 'the greeting'}", Exit 95. Print element 3 of 'the greeting'.

--- LST2-21/24: element 1, plus a variable-index read ---
a list called 'the inbox' is [788, 826, 914].
If element 1 of 'the inbox' is not 788 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-21: expected 788 got {element 1 of 'the inbox'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'the inbox'.
a number called 'the inbox chosen position' is 2.
If element 'the inbox chosen position' of 'the inbox' is not 826 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-24: expected 826 got {element 'the inbox chosen position' of 'the inbox'}", Exit 95. Print element 'the inbox chosen position' of 'the inbox'.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a list called 'the inbox' is [788, 826, 914],
  If element 1 of 'the inbox' is not 788 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-21: expected 788 got {element 1 of 'the inbox'}", Exit 95. Print element 1 of 'the inbox',
  a number called 'the inbox chosen position' is 2,
  If element 'the inbox chosen position' of 'the inbox' is not 826 then, Print "ASSERT LST2-24: expected 826 got {element 'the inbox chosen position' of 'the inbox'}", Exit 95. Print element 'the inbox chosen position' of 'the inbox'.

